.SH NAME
anpu-history - See your past scans


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu history [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List stored scans from the local history database
(~/.anpu/anpu.db) — the same source \fBanpu show\fR and \fBanpu diff\fR read.

.PP
--target filters by target substring (case-insensitive); --json prints
machine-readable rows with full IDs and targets (no truncation).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for history

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print rows as JSON with full IDs and targets

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=20
	maximum number of scans to list

.PP
\fB--target\fP=""
	only list scans whose target contains this substring


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


